hadiths[27]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16256","Hushaym narrated to us from Yala ibn Ata from his father from Aws ibn Aws al-Thaqafi, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) come to a cistern of a people and perform ablution."
"16257","He said: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us from Shubah from al-Numan ibn Salim from Ibn Abi Aws from his grandfather that his sandals used to be brought to him while he was praying, and he would wear them and say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in his sandals."
"16258","He said: Yahya narrated to us from Shubah, he said: Yala ibn Ata narrated to us from his father from Aws ibn Abi Aws, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe over his sandals, then stand for prayer."
"16259","He said: Yahya narrated to us from Shubah, he said: Yala ibn Ata narrated to us from his father from Aws ibn Abi Aws, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and wipe over his sandals, then stand for prayer."
"16260","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us from al-Numan, he said: I heard Aws saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the delegation of Thaqif, and we were in a dome. Everyone in it stood except me and other than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then a man came and spoke to him privately, and he said: Go and kill him. Then he said: Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah? He said: Yes, but he says it seeking protection. He said: Send him back. Then he said: I was commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah; when they say it, their blood and their wealth become inviolable to me except by its right. I said to Shubah: Is it not in the hadith: Then he said: Does he not testify that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah? Shubah said: I think it is with it, and I do not know."
"16261","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed us from Umar ibn Muhammad from Said ibn Abi Hilal from Muhammad ibn Said from Aws ibn Aws from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When it is Friday, and one of you washes his head and bathes, then goes early or goes in the morning, then draws near and listens and is silent, he will have for every step he takes the like of fasting a year and standing a year."
"16262","He said: Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani from Aws ibn Aws, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the best of your days is Friday; in it Adam was created, in it he was taken, in it is the Blast and in it is the Swoon. So send much blessings upon me in it, for your blessings are presented to me. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how will our blessings be presented to you when you have decayed, meaning: when you have perished? He said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic is He, has prohibited the earth from eating the bodies of the prophets, may the blessings of Allah be upon them."
"16263","He said: Abdullah ibn Bakr al-Sahmi narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Abi Saghir narrated to us from al-Numan ibn Salim that Amr ibn Aws informed him that his father Aws informed him, he said: While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in al-Suffah, while he was narrating to us and reminding us, a man came and spoke to him privately. He said: Go and kill him. He said: When the man turned away, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called him. He said: Does he testify that there is no god but Allah? The man said: Yes, yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Go and let him go, for I was only commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no god but Allah; when they do that, their blood and their wealth become inviolable to me except by its right."
"16264","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Abu Yunus Hatim ibn Abi Saghir narrated to us, he said: Al-Numan ibn Salim narrated to me that Amr ibn Aws informed him from his father Aws, he said: While we were sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrating to us and advising us, a man came to him, then he mentioned the like of it."
"16265","He said: Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us: Yala ibn Ata informed us from Aws ibn Abi Aws, he said: I saw my father one day perform ablution and wipe over the two sandals, so I said to him: Do you wipe over them? He said: Thus I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
"16266","He said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taifi narrated to us from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Aws al-Thaqafi from his grandfather Aws ibn Hudhayfah, he said: I was in the delegation who came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who embraced Islam, of Thaqif, of Banu Malik. He lodged us in a dome of his, and he used to visit us between his houses and the mosque. When he had prayed the last Isha, he would turn to us, and we would not leave until he narrated to us, and he would complain of Quraysh and complain of the people of Makkah, then say: It is not the same; in Makkah we were humiliated and weakened, and when we left to Madinah the fortunes of war were against us and for us. He stayed away from us one night and did not come to us until that was long for us after Isha. He said: We said: What kept you from us, O Messenger of Allah? He said: A portion of the Quran came upon me, and I wanted not to come out until I completed it. He said: In the morning we asked the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: We said: How do you portion the Quran? They said: We portion it three surahs, five surahs, seven surahs, nine surahs, eleven surahs, thirteen surahs, and the portion of al-Mufassal from Qaf until it is sealed."
"16267","Waki narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us from al-Numan ibn Salim from Ibn Abi Aws from his grandfather that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in his sandals."
"16268","He said: Waki narrated to us from Sharik from Yala ibn Ata from Aws ibn Abi Aws from his father that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped over his sandals."
"16269","He said: Bahz narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us: Al-Numan ibn Salim narrated to us from a man whose grandfather is Aws ibn Abi Aws: He used to pray and gesture to his sandals while in prayer, then take them and wear them and pray in them, and say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in his sandals."
"16270","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us: Shubah narrated to us from al-Numan ibn Salim from Ibn Abi Aws from his grandfather Aws, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and pour water three times, that is, he washed his hands."
"16271","He said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Shubah ibn al-Hajjaj informed us from al-Numan ibn Salim from Ibn Abi Aws from his grandfather Aws, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and pour water three times, meaning he washed his hands three times. I said to Shubah: Did he put them into the vessel or wash them outside? He said: I do not know."
"16272","He said: Husayn ibn Ali al-Jufi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir narrated it to us from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani from Aws ibn Aws, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever washes and bathes, and goes early and comes in the morning, then draws near and listens and does not engage in idle talk, he will have for every step the like of the reward of a year, its fasting and its standing."
"16273","He said: Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from al-Awzai from Hassan ibn Atiyyah from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani from Aws ibn Aws al-Thaqafi, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever washes and bathes on Friday, and goes early in the morning, and walks and does not ride, then draws near the imam and listens and does not engage in idle talk, he will have for every step the deed of a year, the reward of its fasting and its standing."
"16274","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us from al-Awzai, he said: Hassan ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani narrated to me, he said: Aws ibn Aws al-Thaqafi narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then he mentioned the like of it, except that he said: Then he went early in the morning."
"16275","He said: Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Mubarak informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to me, he said: Abu al-Ashath narrated to me, he said: Aws ibn Aws al-Thaqafi narrated to me, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned Friday, and said: Whoever washes and bathes, then goes early in the morning and comes out walking and does not ride, then draws near the imam and is silent and does not engage in idle talk, he will have the like of the reward of a year, its fasting and its standing."
"16276","He said: And Yahya ibn al-Harith claimed that he retained from Abu al-Ashath that he said to him: For every step the like of the reward of a year, its fasting and its standing. Yahya said: And I did not hear him say: He walked and did not ride."
"16277","He said: Al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us from Rashid ibn Dawud al-Sanani from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani from Aws ibn Aws al-Thaqafi from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever bathes on Friday and washes, then comes early in the morning and goes to the mosque, then sits near the imam until he is silent, he will have for every step he takes the deed of a year, its fasting and its standing."
"16278","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us from al-Numan ibn Salim from Ibn Aws, he said: My grandfather Aws would sometimes pray and gesture to me while in prayer, so I would give him his sandals, and he would say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in his sandals."
"16279","He said: Abu Ahmad al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us from Abdullah ibn Isa from Yahya ibn al-Harith from Abu al-Ashath al-Sanani from Aws ibn Aws al-Thaqafi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever washes and bathes, then goes early in the morning and sits near the imam and listens and is silent, for every step is the reward of a year, its fasting and its standing."
"16280","He said: Affan narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Al-Numan ibn Salim narrated to us, he said: I heard so-and-so, Aws, his grandfather, he said: My grandfather would say to me while in prayer, gesturing to me: Hand me the sandals, so I would hand them to him, and he would wear them and pray in them, and say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in his sandals."
"16281","He said: Ali ibn Hafs and Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated to us from al-Numan ibn Salim, he said: I heard Amr ibn Aws narrating from his grandfather Aws ibn Abi Aws that he saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution and pour water three times. He said: I said: What is pouring water three times? He said: He washed his hands three times."
"16282","He said: Al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us from Yala ibn Ata from Aws ibn Abi Aws, he said: I was with my father at one of the waters of the Arabs, and he performed ablution and wiped over his sandals. So it was said to him, and he said: I will not add for you beyond what I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do."
